.TH fmt_8longlong 3
.SH NAME
fmt_8longlong \- write an octal ASCII representation of an unsigned long long integer
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <fmt.h>

size_t \fBfmt_8longlong\fP(char *\fIdest\fR,unsigned long long \fIsource\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
fmt_8longlong writes an ASCII representation ('0' to '7', base 8) of
\fIsource\fR to \fIdest\fR and returns the number of bytes written.  No
leading zeros are written, and no terminating NUL.

If \fIdest\fR is NULL, nothing is written and only the length is returned.

It is the same as fmt_8long(3), but also takes 64-bit values where
unsigned long has 32 bits.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
fmt_8long(3)
